LPA KIV-2: about 29 KIV-2 repeats in total over both copies (95% interval for read sampling, 23.8 to 35.8; aligner or library bias not included): within or overlapping the range most people have (30 to 45 for about 70% of the 1000 Genomes samples) (KIV-2 exons 65.36x, single-copy exons 29.28x, MAPQ 0 share 0.900)
LPA LPA KIV-2 4925G>A (a splice variant that lowers the Lp(a) made from its chromosome, Coassin 2017): present, 7 of 273 reads at its seven GRCh38 copies carry it (about 0.8 of the 31 copies counted). Carriers had a lower Lp(a) than non-carriers with the same number of repeats, most of all with few repeats. A short-read fraction cannot say which chromosome or which repeat carries it, so it cannot say whether it sits on the small or the large isoform.
